# Constructor Behavior (Important Interview Question)

Consider:

```cpp
class Animal {
public:
    Animal() {
        cout << "Animal Constructor\n";
    }
};

class Dog : virtual public Animal {
};

class Cat : virtual public Animal {
};

class Pet : public Dog, public Cat {
};
```

```cpp
Pet p;
```

Output:

```text
Animal Constructor
```

Only once!

Even though:

* Dog inherits Animal
* Cat inherits Animal

Virtual inheritance ensures only one Animal object is created.

